   252	## 4. Attack (i): the sheet-location theorem
   253	
   254	By Cor 3.2 the whole of attack (i) is the single question: **is box `(Y-U, e=1)`
   255	empty?** Three equivalent forms, all proved equivalent here:
   256	
   257	> **Prop 4.1.** The following are equivalent.
   258	> (α) `b = 0`, i.e. every component `B_j` of `B_Y` has `e_j >= 2`;
   259	> (β) `b_p = 0` for every `p ∈ D`, i.e. `a_p = s_p` everywhere and (M) = (M');
   260	> (γ) no dicritical divisor of `F` with affine image is unramified over `A_F`.
   261	> *Proof.* (α)⟹(β): let `y ∈ B_Y`, `q(y) = p`, and pick `p' ∈ D_0` near `p`.
   262	> `q|_{B_Y}` is finite onto `D`, so `B_Y ∩ V_y` is a curve through `y` whose image
   263	> covers a neighbourhood of `p` in `D`; hence some `y' ∈ B_Y ∩ V_y ∩ q^{-1}(p')`,
   264	> with `e_{y'} = e_{j'} >= 2`. Conservation of number gives
   265	> `e_y = sum_{y'' ∈ V_y ∩ q^{-1}(p')} e_{y''} >= 2`. (β)⟹(α) and (α)⟺(γ) are the
   266	> definitions (`B_j` ↔ the divisorial valuation of a dicritical of `F` whose
   267	> center on the target is the curve `D`). ∎
   268	
   269	So the gate is a statement about **dicritical multiplicities**, and it has an
   270	exact analytic reading:
   271	
   272	> **Lemma 4.2 (dicritical multiplicity = order of `dx ∧ dy`).** Let `X` be a
   273	> smooth compactification of `A^2` on which `F` extends to `Phi: X -> P^2`, let
   274	> `L_j ⊂ X \ A^2` be dicritical with `Phi(L_j) = closure(A_F)`, `v_j := ord_{L_j}`.
   275	> Then `e_j = 1 + v_j(dx ∧ dy)`.
   276	> *Proof.* At a generic `p ∈ D` take local target coordinates `(w,t)` with
   277	> `D = {t=0}`; `du ∧ dv = unit * dw ∧ dt`. At a generic point of `L_j` take
   278	> `(xi, z)` with `L_j = {z=0}`. `Phi|_{L_j}` is non-constant onto `D`, so
   279	> `w∘F = W(xi,z)` with `W_xi(xi,0) != 0`; by definition of `e_j`,
   280	> `t∘F = z^{e_j} T` with `T(xi,0) != 0`. Then
   281	> `d(w∘F) ∧ d(t∘F) = e_j z^{e_j - 1} W_xi T * dxi ∧ dz + O(z^{e_j})`, so
   282	> `v_j(F^*(du∧dv)) = e_j - 1`. But `F^*(du∧dv) = Jac(F) * dx∧dy = dx∧dy` up to a
   283	> nonzero constant, by the Keller hypothesis. ∎
   284	
   285	Lemma 4.2 is a genuine gain: it converts "sheet location" into a **numerical
   286	invariant of a divisorial valuation at infinity**, computable from Enriques data.
   287	Writing `v = ord_{E_N}` for a valuation obtained from `P^2` by blowups at
   288	`P_1 ∈ L_inf, P_2, ..., P_N` with multiplicities `c_i = ord_{E_N}(E_i^{tot})`,
   289	
   290	`v(dx ∧ dy) = sum_i c_i - 3 * sum_{i : P_i ∈ strict transform of L_inf} c_i`,
